## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design scalable, auditable cross-account access that bridges SAP authorizations with AWS IAM, while using JIT and MFA in a multi-region, multi-account setup. Tests integration points across IAM, SCPs, SSO, auditing, and basic IaC.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-account trust and least privilege
- SCPs and IAM role mappings to SAP authorizations
- Just‑In‑Time elevation with AWS SSO and MFA
- Auditing: CloudTrail, Config, Central logging
- Minimal IaC for trust role and VPC endpoint service

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Terraform-like snippet for cross-account trust role (pseudo)
provider "aws" { alias = "shared" }
resource "aws_iam_role" "sap_operator_trust" {
  name = "sap-operator-cross-account"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow",
        Principal = { AWS = ["arn:aws:iam::111111111111:root"] },
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole",
        Condition = { StringEquals = { "sts:ExternalId" = "sap-access" } }
      }
    ]
  })
}

// Per‑BU session policy (inline for example)
resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "sap_operator_policy" {
  name = "sap-operator-permission"
  role = aws_iam_role.sap_operator_trust.name
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [
      { Effect = "Allow", Action = ["ec2:Describe*"], Resource = "*" },
      { Effect = "Allow", Action = ["sap:*"], Resource = "*" }
    ]
  })
}

// VPC Endpoint Service placeholder
resource "aws_vpc_endpoint_service" "sap_endpoints" {
  acceptance_required = true
  network_load_balancer_arns = [aws_lb.sap_nlb.arn]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the mapping between SAP authorizations and AWS roles at scale?
- How would you handle key rotation and revocation in this model?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical understanding of cross‑account IAM with MFA, least privilege, and IaC integration in a real SAP on AWS scenario.

## Key Concepts

- STS assumeRole with MFA
- IAM trust policies and cross‑account access
- Least privilege for SAP HANA actions
- Terraform for IAM role and trust policy
- CloudTrail auditing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Terraform: IAM role with MFA‑enforced trust
resource "aws_iam_role" "sap_operator" {
  name = "sap-operator"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = { AWS = "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_B_ID:root" }
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Condition = { aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent = "true" }
      }
    ]
  })
}
```

```javascript
// Terraform: least-privilege SAP actions
resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "sap_operator_policy" {
  name = "sap-operator-policy"
  role = aws_iam_role.sap_operator.id
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Action = ["sap:Read", "sap:Execute"]
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}
```

```javascript
# CLI test: assume role with MFA and perform a harmless SAP action
aws sts assume-role --role-arn arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_A_ID:role/sap_operator --role-session-name sap-test \
  --serial-number arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_B_ID:mfa/user --token-code 123456
``` 

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate ongoing policy least-privilege using AWS Config or IAM Access Analyzer?
- What changes would you make to rotate credentials or rotate the operator role across regions?

